WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.750
count first builds a four-bin histogram with atomics.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:10.260
In route, start counts tokens in earlier categories and rank counts earlier tokens in the same category.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.155
Their sum is a unique stable destination.

00:00:13.155 --> 00:00:18.225
The count and route launches share a stream, so the histogram is ready before route reads it.

00:00:19.725 --> 00:00:21.410
Count categories.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.880
Build counts before routing starts.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.385
Find start and rank.

00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:28.650
Combine the category region and local order.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.925
Write token ID.

00:00:29.925 --> 00:00:32.460
Give each token a unique stable slot.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.070
Device-memory phase results connect counting to placement.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:44.415
Atomics can count safely, but the order of atomic arrivals alone does not preserve token order.

00:00:44.415 --> 00:00:47.855
The explicit earlier-token rank supplies stability.
